    "name": "Dried and cured Inchellium Garlic",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Inchelium Red garlic is&nbsp;a highly regarded softneck variety known for its exceptional flavor and long storage life.&nbsp;Originating from the Colville Indian Reservation in Washington, it boasts a mild but lingering taste that intensifies during storage, making it a versatile culinary choice.&nbsp;Its attractive bulbs, often exhibiting light pink to purple stripes, are large, typically over 3 inches in diameter, and contain 8-20 cloves.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by Camas Swale</span></p>",
